    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter July 4th with a clear emphasis on aggressive baserunning and favorable platoon splits against struggling arms. The standout play of the day is **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13), whose elite sprint speed and top-of-the-order billing against the vulnerable Kyle Leahy create a massive ceiling for stolen base potential. **Christian Yelich** (74.33) follows closely as a primary target; despite a historical BvP drag, his matchup against Merrill Kelly\u2014carrying a 5.47 xERA\u2014provides a prime environment for him to catalyze the offense from the leadoff spot. We also expect strong production from **Trea Turner** (67.06) and **Kyle Schwarber** (66.71), both of whom benefit from positive lineup positioning, though both are tethered to a 42% rain risk that necessitates monitoring as first pitch approaches.\n\nStrategic plate discipline and favorable matchups highlight the remainder of the lineup, with **Caleb Durbin** (65.78) and **Colt Keith** (64.81) both thriving due to strong platoon advantages and the tendency for their opposing pitchers to allow high-frequency stolen base opportunities. **Junior Caminero** (64.07) provides stability in the UTIL slot, maintaining high efficiency despite a tougher matchup against Hunter Brown. The most difficult roster decision involved leaving **Luke Raley** (58.60) on the bench; while his matchup against Shane Bieber is statistically intriguing due to the park factors and platoon edge, **Yordan Alvarez** (58.67) and the high-upside utility options narrowly out-projected him in our optimizer's current model. We remain confident that the combination of **Gary Sanchez**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, **Josh Smith**, and **Casey Schmitt** provides the necessary depth to keep the Zebras competitive across all five categories today.",
